            "position": 0,
            "original": "Bir derdim var",
            "rendering": "I carry this ache",
            "note": "Turkish “dert” has no single English counterpart (trouble? sorrow? burden?). In folk poetry a dert is something you carry and claim — “carry” adds that ownership where “have” stays passive.",
